{"id":"property-value-250k-500k","version":1,"category":"property-value","when":"Approximate US$250,000–500,000 property-value or budget context; flexible design reference only.","title":"Property value reference: Comfortable family living","combinations":"Compose with regional/style, room planning, entrance, facade, roof, materials and climate/site recipes. Waterfront entertaining may justify a pavilion, terraces or pool; urban sites may favor courts and privacy. Recreation, wellness, guest houses and garages are optional.","placement":"Connect arrival to shared living and sheltered outdoor space; protect suite privacy from guest and service routes. Scale and spatial complexity follow programme and site capacity, not a price formula.","principles":"Improve kitchen-dining relationships, storage and household privacy; consider a useful sheltered garden room. Give arrival legibility and use better materials selectively. Price alone determines neither floor area, bedrooms nor amenities. Avoid underdeveloped massing and unjustified scale; assess the actual household brief.","capabilities":"Build real supported floors, coordinated enclosures, room openings, entrance assemblies, roofs and terraces. A luxury label or collection of walls/windows/roof does not establish architectural completeness; cite changed element IDs and disclose missing access/interiors.","construction":{"operations":["add","replace","move","resize","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"supports":"Coordinate supporting enclosure and roof/floor datums atomically; entrances and terraces need actual connections and access.","materials":"Select available materials and facade depth for local character and maintainability; conceptual finishes do not prove craftsmanship.","unsupported":"No valuation, construction-cost estimate, automatic programme, engineering, services, code or luxury certification."}}
